                                            "plural-only"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40e9f932-9365-4b8d-a781-86759bb91cca",
                                                "sense_id": "4531ba14-37dc-37b5-afb6-dd202bdff503",
                                                "text": "We passed through a large Hakka town (Hakka is a Chinese language, one of the three official languages in Taiwan; more on that in later posts) and then began to pitch and roll through a series of white-knuckling switchbacks up Hsinchu County Road 22. About an hour later we landed (which is really the only appropriate verb) in the village of Cingcyuan, an Atayal aboriginal community.[…]\nThat being said, the Atayal of Cingcyuan are among the friendliest people I have met. I wandered through the village market and bought a homemade spicy sausage from a woman tending a barbecue.[…]\n“They are very innocent people,” said Yen Yen “And very generous.” I agreed, wondering when I could come back to Cingcyuan."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
